== NOTES
These are domains, not machine arithmetic: a std::abi::U8 is an ordinary Int
with the proof that it lies in 0..255, held in the struct's one field
`value`. Each type is a nominal struct, so std::abi::u8(255) + 1 is the TYPE
error, never 0 or 256: compute in Int (x.value), and re-enter a domain
through its creator. std::abi::I32 and std::abi::U32 are distinct even where
they overlap, as are std::abi::I64 and std::abi::Isize. Machine meaning
(sign or zero extension into a register) starts only at an architecture
layer, std::abi::x86_64::from_i32 and its siblings. C's own integer types
are std::ffi::c's.

