== NOTES
Two intrinsics, no module file. A byte storage is a runtime value kind of
its own: an immutable, finite sequence of bytes with an exact length, no
terminator, compared and hashed by its bytes. No source type spells it (its
static type is any); std::abi::bytes::Bytes is the opaque struct whose one
field holds one, and only module std::abi::bytes can construct or open a
Bytes. So programs use std::abi::bytes::from_list and
std::abi::bytes::length; these intrinsics are what that module is written
in. There is deliberately no operation that reads, slices or iterates the
bytes.

