== NOTES
The text a DecimalRounded value guarantees, never the digits of the
binary64 behind it: x rounded half to even to the N places of its static
type (DecimalRounded{minDecimalsPreserved: N}), written with exactly N
digits after the point -- trailing zeros kept, no point at N = 0 -- and a
"-" only before a nonzero result (DecimalRounded has no negative zero:
-0.04 at one place is "0.0"). It is the same text a program's printed
result shows. The precision is the argument's static type's: the compiler
writes it into the call, so a value carries none, and a value weakened to
fewer places shows those (a DecimalRounded{minDecimalsPreserved: 3} value
