== DESCRIPTION
The namespace's intrinsics are root natives registered under their qualified
names -- std::float64::from_int, std::float64::truncate,
std::float64::from_decimal_rounded (core/float.tcl, FLOAT64-MILESTONE-1.md)
-- and this module may never define a member of the same name
(surface/modules.tcl, DUPLICATE-NATIVE; STDLIB-NAMESPACES.md). Below are the
comparisons every program that bounds a Float64 writes, added by the Icy
Tower workload (ICY-TOWER-VERTICAL-SLICE-1.md, "Stdlib additions"):

  std::float64::min(a, b)            the smaller of A and B (A when they
                                     are equal)
  std::float64::max(a, b)            the larger of A and B (A when they
                                     are equal)
  std::float64::abs(x)               X without its sign
  std::float64::clamp(x, low, high)  X bounded to LOW..HIGH: LOW when X is
                                     below it, else HIGH when X is above
                                     that, else X

Each is a comparison and at most a negation, so none can fail: there is no
arithmetic that could leave the finite Float64s (no NonFiniteFloat), and a
Float64 has no NaN for a comparison to be unordered with. min and max are
`nomethod`: their operands are symmetric, and neither is a receiver (the
bit_and precedent, REFACTOR-WARNINGS-CLEAN.md).

